{"ticker":"VINATIORGA","symbol":"VINATIORGA","instrumentId":3119047,"name":"Vinati Organics","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Specialty","about":"Vinati Organics is a prominent manufacturer of specialty chemicals and organic intermediates, catering to diverse industries such as pharmaceuticals, agrochemicals, personal care, and water treatment. The company’s product portfolio includes ATBS (2-Acrylamido 2-Methylpropane Sulfonic Acid), IBB (Iso Butyl Benzene), and other value-added products that are critical raw materials for various applications. With state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities in India, Vinati Organics focuses on quality, innovation, and sustainable production processes. The company exports a significant portion of its output, serving customers across 35+ countries. Vinati Organics emphasizes environmental responsibility and continuous research, driving growth through advanced chemical solutions that meet global standards.","website":"www.vinatiorganics.com","location":"Raigad, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T14:08:56.366Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":1173.2,"changePct":2.150631258162825,"week52High":1624,"week52Low":953.65},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹12,162 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹2,511 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"26,953,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"113"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"13,107,513"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.72%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"3.85"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.8"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.12"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.82"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"5%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"29.52"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"32–71"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"14.0%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"53.81"},{"label":"Volume","value":"30,783"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"66,208"},{"label":"Master score","value":"35"},{"label":"EPS ra